Arthur, you are here to prepare for your journey, not to play with trinkets of wealth.	亞瑟，你來此是為了準備啟程，不是來把玩這些身外財物的。
The trap door is already open.	活板門已經開著了。
That is the Treasurer's only source of light.	那是司庫唯一的光源。
You could, if you were holding it.	你若拿著它，倒是可以。
There is too much metal all around and it confuses the workings of the lodestone.	四周金屬太多，擾亂了指北針的運作。
The Treasurer needs it more than you do.	司庫比你更需要它。
You have no business doing that until you know Gawaine is dead.	在確知高文已死之前，你無權這麼做。
I am sure you could find one anywhere in Camelot if you looked hard enough.	我相信只要你用心找，在肯萊特任何角落都能找到一個。
When you have seen one rodent, you have seen them all.	見過一隻齧齒動物，便等於見過牠們全部。
You have more important things to think about.	你還有更要緊的事該想。
Is this some sort of odd Pictish word?	這是某種古怪的皮克特語詞彙嗎？
Which one first, m'lord?	吾王，先要哪一種？
Coins of tin?  Never heard'o such a thing.	錫幣？老朽從未聽聞這種東西。
We have no coins made of bronze, sire.	陛下，我們沒有青銅鑄造的錢幣。
You have coins already, my king, but if you wish to change them, please give me the purse.	我王，你已經有錢幣了，但若你想兌換，請把錢囊交給我。
Aye, gladly, if you will but provide me with the purse to fill.	是，樂意之至，只要你把錢囊交給我裝滿。
Your purse is full, my liege.	吾主，你的錢囊已經滿了。
I have no purse to give you. If you have brought your own, I can fill it for you.	我沒有錢囊可以給你。你若帶著自己的，我可以替你裝滿。
But you have it, sire.	但陛下，錢囊在你身上。
I have no purse to give you, m'lord.	吾王，我沒有錢囊可以給你。
You must come closer, m'lord.	你得再靠近些，吾王。
Here you are, m'lord, but the purse is empty. I beg you to let me fill it for you ere you go.	拿去吧，吾王，但錢囊是空的。趁你尚未啟程，容我為你裝滿。
There is room for more, m'lord, but here it is, as you command.	還裝得下更多，吾王，但既然你這麼吩咐，錢囊便交給你了。
Here it is, m'lord, as you command.	遵命奉上，吾王。
Steal?  But, my lord, it is already yours.	偷？可是，吾王，這東西本就是你的。
But, m'lord, you have coins in your purse. Still, if you wish to change what you have, you have but to give me the purse again.	可是，吾王，你的錢囊裡已經有錢幣了。不過，你若想兌換手上的錢，儘管把錢囊再給我便是。
What coins would you be wantin', m'lord?	吾王想要哪種錢幣？
Your purse is full and I have no other purses or bags to fill.	你的錢囊已經滿了，我也沒有別的錢囊或袋子可裝了。
Travelling with bulging moneybags would only bring bandits and outlaws down upon you like a plague of locusts.	帶著鼓脹的錢袋上路，只會招來強盜與亡命之徒，如蝗蟲過境般撲向你。
Take your purse and cease badgering your Treasurer. He is wise in these matters and greed does not become a King.	拿好你的錢囊，別再纏著你的司庫了。他深諳此道，貪婪可配不上一位國王。
I have it in hand, m'lord. I await your commands.	已在我手中，吾王，靜候你的吩咐。
You do not have the purse with you, Arthur.	亞瑟，你身上並沒有帶著錢囊。
Thank you, m'lord. I shall fill it according to your wishes.	多謝，吾王，我這就依你的心意裝滿它。
I have emptied the purse, so we may begin again. What is your command?	我已將錢囊倒空，可以重新開始了。你有何吩咐？
No need to give me money, m'lord. You reward me well enough.	不必給我錢，吾王，你待我已經夠厚了。
You must get money before you can give money.	你得先有錢，才能給人錢。
I am the one who should be giving you money, m'lord. What are your commands?	該給你錢的人是我，吾王。你有何吩咐？
I have no need to take any for myself. You reward me well enough already.	我用不著為自己拿一分一毫，你待我已經夠厚了。
As you wish. Give me the purse, then.	悉聽尊便。那麼，把錢囊給我吧。
You do not even have the purse.	你連錢囊都沒帶在身上。
The purse is empty, m'lord. I await your commands.	錢囊是空的，吾王，靜候你的吩咐。
There are silver coins in your purse.	你的錢囊裡有銀幣。
You now have gold coins, my King.	我王，你現在有金幣了。
I have given you copper coins, m'lord.	吾王，我已經給了你銅幣。
The purse has coins in it, m'lord, but if that is your wish...	錢囊裡已經有錢幣了，吾王，但既然這是你的心意……
The purse is now empty. What is your command?	錢囊現在是空的。你有何吩咐？
Ah, a good luck charm! I thank you, m'lord.	啊，一個護身符！多謝，吾王。
Ah, a good luck charm!	啊，一個護身符！
Here you are, m'lord.	拿去吧，吾王。
My king, if you seek my advice, I say this -- take with you coins of all three value: copper, silver and gold. Each has its use.	我王，若你想聽我的建言，我要說：三種面額的錢幣都該帶上——銅、銀、金，各有各的用處。
If you have brought your purse with you, m'lord, I will be happy to fill it for you.	你若帶著錢囊來，吾王，我很樂意為你裝滿。
I am here to serve you as I may, though, to speak bluntly, I hope you will soon be in search of the Grail.	我在此盡我所能為你效勞，不過老實說，我盼你早日踏上尋找聖杯的旅程。
Please tell me how I may serve you.	請告訴我該如何為你效勞。
Hands that shed innocent blood will never touch the Grail.	沾染無辜鮮血的雙手，永遠碰不到聖杯。
He is your loyal servant.  Why would you want to fight him?	他是你忠心的僕人，你為何想跟他動手？
Gar!  Keep away, you pox-cursed pooftah!	哼！滾開，你這染上瘡病的斷袖孽徒！
Where I come from, that is not a manly thing to do.	在我的家鄉，這可不是男子漢該做的事。
Pardon me, Sire, but that would take months.	恕罪，陛下，但那得花上數月光陰。
It was sealed by Sir Gawaine when he left it here, and he charged me to see that the seal is not broken except by his own hand...unless he is dead.	這是高文爵士離去時親手封上的，他囑咐我務必守著，除非他親自解封……或是他已經身故。
Nay, leave it be. Your mission must be kept humble, for safety as well as your soul's sake.	不可，別去動它。你的使命必須保持謙卑，這既是為了安全，也是為了你的靈魂。
By your leave, m'lord, I keep it open so that fresh air may enter the room.  And so the mice may leave it.	容稟，吾王，我讓它開著，好讓新鮮空氣進來房裡，也好讓老鼠有路可出去。
Those bundles belong to Sir Gawaine. They are all his worldly possessions which he left in my keeping, for I was the last man to see him ere he left.	那些包裹是高文爵士的。那是他所有的身外之物，他離去前交由我保管，因為我是他啟程前見到的最後一人。
I have it, Sire, and await your instructions.	已在我手中，陛下，靜候你的指示。
The bags contain gold and silver cups and platters and other booty from the battles you have won.	袋裡裝的是金杯銀盤，以及你征戰得勝所獲的其他戰利品。
Each jar before me is filled with coins: one with gold coins, one with silver coins and one with copper coins.	我面前的每個罐子都裝滿了錢幣：一罐金幣、一罐銀幣、一罐銅幣。
Greetings, my King.  The jar to your left contains copper coins, the jar in the center holds silver coins and the jar to your right is filled with gold coins.	見過我王。你左手邊的罐子裝著銅幣，中間的罐子裝著銀幣，右手邊的罐子則裝滿金幣。
One gold coin is worth 5 silver coins or 25 copper coins.	一枚金幣值五枚銀幣，或二十五枚銅幣。
You have forgotten my name after years of service? Awr, you are having a joke. Hawrh! Hawrh! Hawrh!	小人伺候陛下多年，陛下竟忘了小人的名字？啊呀，陛下真會說笑。哈！哈！哈！
I was the last to see Sir Gawaine.  He made sure to take copper coins along with silver and gold.  He told me he planned to search for the Grail in the ruins of Glastonbury Tor.	我是最後見到高文爵士的人。他特意帶上了銅幣，連同銀幣與金幣一起。他告訴我，他打算前往格列斯登伯利山的廢墟尋找聖杯。
That is the last that I, or any man, has heard of him.	那便是我，或任何人，最後聽聞他的消息了。
I wish I could tell you something useful, m'lord.	但願我能告訴你些有用的事，吾王。
In memory of Graham Chapman	謹以此紀念葛拉罕·查普曼。
I pray to all the powers that be that you will return safely, that the Grail will be yours, as surely it must be.	我向天地間的一切神靈祈求，願你平安歸來，願聖杯終將屬於你，此事必成。
And may you find and bring back all the noble knights who have gone before you on this holy mission.	也願你尋回、帶回所有先你踏上這神聖使命、卻杳無音訊的高貴騎士。
Your fate will be always in my mind during the long and lonely hours.	在那些漫漫長夜、形單影隻的時刻，我心中將永遠掛念你的命運。
I will add prayers for your return to those I have already made everyday for Sir Launcelot.	我會在每日已為蘭斯洛特爵士祈禱之外，再加上為你平安歸來的祈禱。
And Sir Gawaine and Sir Galahad, of course.	當然，還有高文爵士與葛拉漢爵士。
There is no more I can bear to say.  Dally no more with me, my lord.  Fare thee well.	我再也說不下去了。莫再與我流連，吾王，願你一路平安。
A lodestone?  I have no need of it, but you surely might.  I insist you keep it.	一個指北針？我用不著，但你想必用得上，我堅持要你收下。
But it is I who give it to you.  I have whispered secrets to it and nourished it with my tears.  It is imbued with the power of my love.	但這是我要送給你的東西。我曾對它低語心事，以淚水滋養它，它已注滿了我愛的力量。
Indeed not, husband.  That would be most undignified.	確實不會，夫君，那樣未免太失體統。
I will cherish those words always.	這些話，我將永遠珍藏在心。
I have for you all the loving devotion a wife could have for a husband.	我對你懷有妻子對丈夫所能付出的一切摯愛與忠貞。
Girl?  I am Gwenhyver -- your queen, your woman, your wife.  I am no girl.	女孩？我是昆海兒——你的王后、你的女人、你的妻子。我不是什麼女孩。
Is this some sort of odd Moorish word?	這是某種古怪的摩爾語詞彙嗎？
Goodbye, my love.  May you fulfill your destiny.	再會了，我的愛人。願你完成你的天命。
There is no need to steal that which is already yours.	本就屬於你的東西，無須用偷的。
It is written in the Liber ex Doctrina.	這寫在《Liber ex Doctrina》裡。
Alas, my husband, all but one of my roses has withered and fallen.  My garden is dying, even as our kingdom slowly dies.	唉，夫君，我的玫瑰已全數凋零墜落，只剩最後一朵。我的花園正在枯萎，一如我們的國家正緩緩走向衰亡。
We are completely private within these walls.  You need not worry about the window behind us.  Within is only a sewing room and empty at present.	這幾道牆內完全屬於我們的私密之地，你不必擔心身後那扇窗。裡頭只是間縫紉室，此刻空無一人。
There is nothing inside save the ladies' sewing room, of no interest to a warrior.	裡頭除了女眷的縫紉室之外別無他物，對一名戰士毫無意趣。
My fountain is as parched and dry as the lakes and rivers of our poor kingdom.	我的噴泉，如同我們可憐王國裡的湖泊與河流一般，乾涸枯竭。
It is a stone bench and not very comfortable.	這是一張石凳，並不怎麼舒適。
You planted that tree for me when Camelot was first built.  I pray it will survive.	肯萊特初建成時，你為我種下了那棵樹。我祈禱它能撐過這一切。
Wear it next to your heart. In time of need, it will guide you through danger if you recite the Message of the Rose.	把它戴在貼近心口之處。危難之時，只要你誦念玫瑰箴言，它便會指引你穿越險境。
You have taken the only rose.	你已經摘走了僅存的那朵玫瑰。
It is the last and most beautiful of my red roses.  It would please me if you took it as a token of my love.	這是我最後、也是最美的一朵紅玫瑰。你若肯收下它，當作我愛的信物，我會很欣慰。
If I knew the least thing, I would gladly tell you.	我若知道哪怕一丁點消息，也會樂意告訴你。
Ah...uhmmm....we are just good friends.	啊……呃……我們只是好朋友。
However, it is true that I was the last person to talk to him before he went seeking the Grail.  He said he would seek information from the Lady of the Lake.	不過，確實是我最後與他交談——就在他啟程尋找聖杯之前。他說他打算向湖中女神打聽消息。
The watery tart.	那水裡的蕩婦罷了。
It is your Book of Lore, full of many things you need to know, including the Message of the Rose.	這是你的智典，裡頭記載著你需要知曉的諸多事物，包括玫瑰箴言。
I would gladly speak more, but I beg you to delay not another moment in beginning your mission.	我很樂意再多說些，但求你莫再遲延片刻，速速展開你的使命。
Move closer to her.	再靠近她一些。
Her lips do not reach that far.	她的唇夠不到那麼遠。
Nay, Arthur.  You must go now, before the sin of lust makes you unworthy to find the Grail!	不可，亞瑟。你必須立刻離開，免得色慾之罪讓你失去尋得聖杯的資格！
Get a little closer.	再靠近一點。
As nice as this is, Arthur, it does not further your mission.	這固然美好，亞瑟，但無助於你的使命。
Violence in the soul will place the Grail forever beyond your reach.	心中一旦有了暴戾之氣，聖杯便將永遠遙不可及。
Jealousy is a poison to the heart and does not become your noble character.	嫉妒是侵蝕人心的毒藥，配不上你高貴的品格。
Really, husband.  There will be time enough for that if....I mean, when you return.	真是的，夫君。等你……我是說，等你歸來之後，有的是時間做這些事。
Truly, if you wish to help me and your kingdom, you will search for the Grail at once!	你若真心想幫助我與你的王國，此刻就該立刻啟程尋找聖杯！
Such delights must wait until you have returned with the Grail.	這樣的歡愉，得等你帶著聖杯歸來之後才行。
You have no good reason to insult the woman you love and your queen.	你沒有理由這樣侮辱你所愛的女人，也是你的王后。
Gwenhyver looks puzzled.  I know I am.	昆海兒露出困惑的神情。老實說，我也是。
There is only one rose left in her garden, but I have no doubt she would be glad for you to have it.	她的花園裡只剩最後一朵玫瑰，但我毫不懷疑，她會樂意讓你擁有它。
Why what?  Why do we live?  Why do we die?  If you wish to ask me about something specific, fine.  Otherwise, save the sweeping philosophical questions for another time.	為什麼什麼？為什麼我們活著？為什麼我們終將一死？你若想問些具體的事，儘管問。否則，這種漫無邊際的哲學問題，還是留到別的時候再說吧。
Aye, the sky is overhead as usual.	是的，天空一如往常懸在頭頂。
Your land is cursed and only the Grail can heal it.	你的國土受了詛咒，唯有聖杯能夠治癒它。
The ground is made of soil, as most ground is.	這地面由泥土構成，如同大多數地面一樣。
There are no berries, only dying leaves.	沒有漿果，只有正在枯萎的葉子。
Gwenhyver awaits you in her bower.  The blight on Camelot has not spared this place, once the most beautiful garden in the land.	昆海兒在她的花園裡等著你。肯萊特的枯朽之災，也沒有放過這裡——曾是全國最美的花園。
Without the queen here, this dying bower is a sad and empty place.	沒有王后在此，這座垂死的花園顯得格外淒涼、空蕩。
They are such gossips. And none are pure in heart as your queen.	她們最愛說長道短。而且沒有一個像你的王后那樣心地純正。
If there is any news of Launcelot, Gwenhyver is bound to know it.	若有蘭斯洛特的消息，昆海兒必定知曉。
But she's gone.	但她已經不在了。
She is no longer here. Perhaps she went to the Chapel to pray for your success.	她已不在此處。或許她去了神殿，為你的成功祈禱。
She's not here.	她不在這裡。
The bushes are dying from the curse upon Camelot.	這些灌木正因肯萊特所受的詛咒而枯萎。
The walls, not surprisingly, are made of grey stone.	這些牆，不出所料，是灰石砌成的。
